  "branch": "evisdren/pr-603-missing-workspace",
  "effective_engine": "bm25_lexical",
  "facts": [],
  "query": "compact v1 transcript parser shared library import entiredb",
  "retrieval_engine": {
    "schema_version": 1,
    "effective_engine": "bm25_lexical",
    "identity_verified": true,
    "semantic_requested": false,
    "semantic_applied": false,
    "semantic_available": false,
    "bm25_enabled": true,
    "bm25_applied": true,
    "fallback_used": false
  },
  "warnings": [
    "memory count does not match the manifest: 24725 declared, 24732 readable; the manifest is behind the store — run `entire brain refresh`"
  ]
}
[
 {
  "text": "Reports of models \"ignoring\" the brain were determined to be a parser bug in the evaluation harness failing to catch `mcp_tool_call` events.",
  "paths": [
   "constraints.invariants.general"
  ]
 },
 {
  "text": "Entire\u2019s parser failed to generate prompt summaries for the Codex transcript format used in the Linear integration sessions, although the stored raw transcripts contained the prompts; verify raw transcript contents when checking checkpoint completeness.",
  "paths": [
   "workflow.checkpoints.verification"
  ]
 },
 {
  "text": "The brain must reuse platform infrastructure rather than introduce its own: shared storage, crypto, and git metadata belong to decentralized-architecture because they serve multiple consumers.",
  "paths": [
   "architecture.boundaries.rationale"
  ]
 },
 {
  "text": "Brain's \"project-file semantic index\" is not Brain's own parser \u2014 entire-graph parses the repo and Brain ingests Graph's snapshot into its own semantic.sqlite store (~100\u2013200 MB). Brain serves the materialized copy via brief sections and MCP inspect tools (brain_code_context, brain_impact_analysis, ",
  "paths": [
   "architecture.boundaries.rationale"
  ]
 },
 {
  "text": "Embedding entire-judge inside entire-brain to reuse unexported helpers was rejected because the requested plugin must have its own repository and module, like entire-sem; it should consume brain data from disk without importing brain internals, and the embedded approach should be revisited only if t",
  "paths": [
   "architecture.boundaries.rationale"
  ]
 },
 {
  "text": "Publishing SubagentLink.TranscriptPath was rejected because child transcripts remained on the unpushed shadow branch, leaving dangling references in server/UI metadata; use AgentID as the child link and revisit transcript paths only when child transcript promotion to the pushed checkpoint branch exi",
  "paths": [
   "architecture.data.flow"
  ]
 },
 {
  "text": "COR-785 was excluded from the brain Keystone scope because server-side tamper-evident causality links serve platform trust and compliance, while brain can query entity history without them; revisit when the entiredb/hosted P1 rails are merged and shared audit provenance is needed.",
  "paths": [
   "architecture.boundaries.rationale"
  ]
 },
 {
  "text": "A shared connection-gate abstraction for status and sync was considered and rejected because the overlap was only two reads and an environment check, while sync performs side effects and status assembles a report; revisit if substantially more shared decision logic develops.",
  "paths": [
   "architecture.boundaries.rationale"
  ]
 },
 {
  "text": "Direct local v2 raw transcript export was considered and left unchanged because v2 stores compact transcript.jsonl blobs rather than raw full.jsonl blobs, and the existing fallback to CLI explain preserves raw export; revisit if release requirements demand direct local raw mode or the fallback cause",
  "paths": [
   "architecture.data.flow"
  ]
 },
 {
  "text": "The original \u201c9/9 wins\u201d conclusion was rejected because product code embedded benchmark answers and candidate-only task setup leaked targets; reconsider the comparison only with answer recognizers removed, blind shared task definitions, and verified Brain use.",
  "paths": [
   "workflow.testing.rules"
  ]
 }
]

